1
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:27,818
Life made him tough. Love made him strong. Music made him hard.

2
00:08:43,636 --> 00:08:49,636
Walk Hard: The Dewey Cox Story is a comedy, music film directed by Jake Kasdan.

3
00:13:05,454 --> 00:13:11,454
Following a childhood tragedy, Dewey Cox follows a
long and winding road to music stardom.

4
00:17:27,272 --> 00:17:33,272
Dewey perseveres through changing musical styles, an addiction to
nearly every drug known and bouts of uncontrollable rage.

5
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:55,090
Dewey Cox, played by John C. Reilly.

6
00:26:10,909 --> 00:26:16,909
Darlene Madison, played by Jenna Fischer.

7
00:30:32,727 --> 00:30:38,727
Pa Cox, played by Raymond J. Barry.

8
00:34:54,545 --> 00:35:00,545
Edith, played by Kristen Wiig.

9
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
Sam, played by Tim Meadows.

10
00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
L'Chaim, played by Harold Ramis.

11
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Walk Hard: The Dewey Cox Story is a 2007 American musical comedy film directed by
Jake Kasdan, and written by Kasdan and co-producer Judd Apatow.

12
00:52:21,818 --> 00:52:27,818
It stars John C.

13
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
Reilly, Kristen Wiig, Tim Meadows and Jenna Fischer.

14
01:01:05,454 --> 01:01:11,454
A parody of the biopic genre, Walk Hard is the story of a fictional
country music, rock and roll, and folk star played by Reilly.

15
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Walk Hard primarily references the musical biopics Ray (2004) and Walk the Line (2005); in addition to Ray Charles and Johnny Cash, the "Dewey Cox" character includes elements of the lives and careers of other notable
musicians including Roy Orbison, Glen Campbell, Bob Dylan, Jerry Lee Lewis, Donovan, John Lennon, James Brown, Jim Morrison, Conway Twitty, Neil Diamond, Hank Williams, Sonny & Cher and Brian Wilson.

16
01:09:49,090 --> 01:09:55,090
The film portrays fictional versions of artists Buddy Holly, the Big Bopper, Elvis Presley, and the
Beatles; some artists appear as themselves, including Eddie Vedder, Jewel and Ghostface Killah.

17
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
In addition, the film parodies or pays tribute to the musical styles of David Bowie,
Billy Joel, Van Dyke Parks, the Gun Club, and seventies punk rock.

18
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
The film was released in North America on December
21, 2007 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

19
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
It received positive reviews from critics but was a box office disappointment, grossing only
$20.6 million against a $35 million budget; it has since become a cult film.

20
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
The film explores themes of rock 'n' roll, hip-hop, music record, pop star, pop.

21
01:31:38,181 --> 01:31:44,181
The tone is lighthearted.
